{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n13 MB of research artefacts (65 `.py`, 39 md, 36 jsonl, 30 json, 17 yaml) live under `docs/experiments/`; `docs/calibration/` holds 4 notes plus `plan_v5_rescore.py`. Living under `docs/` makes them docs-tooling link-check targets and is the ONLY reason CodeQL skips them. Packaging is confirmed non-shipping: wheel `packages = [\"src/rebar\"]` (`pyproject.toml:363-367`), sdist `include` (`:391`), no `MANIFEST.in`. `scripts/check_docs_index.py` indexes `docs/*.md` (`:70-88`) and link-checks `docs` recursively (`:103`), so after the move it stops seeing the tree. Cites verified on `aa37a738570`.\n\n## Approach\n`git mv docs/experiments evals && git mv docs/calibration evals/calibration` (history preserved), then repoint every live reference OUTSIDE the moved tree.\n\n**The moved tree's own contents are frozen as authored and are NOT repointed.** 61 files / 157 lines inside `docs/experiments/**` and `docs/calibration/**` embed the literal old paths — harness scripts, run artefacts (`runs/*.jsonl`, `*.json`), eval-spec fixtures and research notes. Those strings record what was actually executed, so rewriting them would falsify the research record, exactly as for `docs/archive/`. `evals/` is therefore excluded from the AC2 grep.\n\n**The worklist is the Testing grep, not a hand-kept list.** Three successive hand enumerations each missed live references, so the plan defines the target by that command and AC2 enforces it. Current content: 34 hits in 21 test files and the non-test sites below.\n\n- **`rebar.toml`** `:51` (a `docs/calibration/completion_floor.md` comment), `:216` (comment) and `:220` (`[llm.evals] corpus_root`, which flips to `\"evals\"`).\n- **`.gitignore`** `:19`, `:122` (a comment naming `replay/corpus-*.manifest.json`) and `:123`.\n- **CodeQL — load-bearing, not cosmetic.** `.github/codeql/codeql-config.yml`'s whole ignore list is `docs/**` (`:8-9`); the `docs/experiments` string it once named is gone. The research tree is excluded ONLY by living under `docs/`, so moving it to a top-level `evals/` drops it out of that umbrella and CodeQL would start scanning the 65 research `.py` files. `evals/**` must be added under `paths-ignore` in THIS change.\n- **Live docs under `docs/`**: `architecture.md:312`, `plan-review-gate.md:126,142,198,281,473,1537,1562,1804`, `remediation-implementation-plan.md:180,188,306`, `review-kernel.md:35`. `docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md:8` is GENERATED from `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_A1.md:10`; repoint the reviewer source and regenerate rather than editing the guide.\n- **A SECOND worklist axis the grep cannot see: relative markdown links.** `docs/*.md` links into the trees as `](experiments/...)` / `](calibration/...)`, with no `docs/` prefix, so AC2 can print nothing while every link still points at the vacated paths and `check_docs_index.py`'s recursive link check breaks. Six such lines: `README.md:129,141` (7 links), `architecture.md:310,312`, `llm-framework.md:80,81`. Each becomes `](../evals/...)`. Find them with `git grep -n '](experiments/\\|](calibration/' -- 'docs/*.md'`; AC7 enforces the link check.\n- **Source and packaged data**: `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_A1.md:10` (\"a path under `evals/` (formerly `docs/experiments/`)\"); `src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json` `_comment`s at `:4,92,112,158,189,197,205`; `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_advisory.py:164` and `det_operator_attested.py:11`; `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/corpus.py:5` and `legacy_v4_baseline.py:2-6`; `src/rebar/llm/config_readers.py` (the `[llm.evals]` comment); the six eval-spec comments plus `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/README.plan-review.md:67`; `scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py:45`, `scripts/check_dco_identity.py:30`, `scripts/calibrate_completion_floor.py:9`.\n- **NOT repointed because they carry no such string** (verified): `src/rebar/grounding/resolve.py` and `src/rebar/llm/structured.py` have zero `docs/experiments`/`docs/calibration` matches; `tests/unit/gold_set_completion.py` likewise. All three are dropped from the worklist.\n- **Tests** — 21 files, 34 hits; the grep above is the worklist. Four sites need care beyond a path swap: `test_impact_model_versioning.py` has TWO loaders (`:41`, and `:146` targeting `ab_impact_model.py`); `test_transition_force_flag_24f7.py` has four hits (`:148,149,150,153`), not two; `test_code_review_criteria_routing.py:140` asserts `superseded_by == \"docs/experiments/code-review-threshold-calibration-code-v5.md\"` and must move in step with `criteria_routing.json:4,158`; and `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_removed_cli_verbs_heldout.py:44` holds a `_HISTORY_PREFIXES` entry `docs/experiments/` that becomes a stale prefix once the live tree leaves that path.\n- **Sequencing on `d279` (`disgusted-fretful-hare`, closed).** It added `tests/unit/evals/test_evals_corpus_root.py::test_no_hard_coded_roots`, which asserts `corpus.py` is the SOLE `docs/experiments` match under `src/rebar/llm/evals` (its AC1). Repointing `corpus.py:5` empties that grep and fails the assertion. This change rewrites that module to target the moved tree: the assertion AND the three old-path literals it still carries at `:5` (module docstring), `:96` (test docstring) and `:102` (the grep command string) — AC2 does not exclude `tests/unit/evals`, so leaving them fails it. Also new in `d279` and in scope: `tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_cli_paths.py` (module docstring) and `config_readers.py` above.\n- `evals/calibration/plan_v5_rescore.py` keeps importing `rebar.llm.evals.plan_replay.legacy_v4_baseline` (research-to-src, unchanged); `legacy_v4_baseline.py` stays the importable home of the v4 formula because `evals/` is not on `sys.path`.\n\n## Scope\nThe moved trees; `rebar.toml`; `.gitignore`; `.github/codeql/codeql-config.yml`; the 3 scripts, the source/packaged-data files, the live docs, and the 20 test files enumerated above. Parent epic `e47b` AC2 carries the identical historical carve-outs, so leaf and parent agree. Deliberately NOT repointed: the moved tree's own 157 internal references (frozen as authored, above), `docs/adr/` (6 refs), `docs/archive/`, `docs/research/`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `docs/release-notes.md`, `tests/fixtures/`, and generated `.test_durations`. AC2's grep excludes exactly that set.\n\n## Testing\n`python scripts/check_docs_index.py`; `python scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py`; `python evals/calibration/plan_v5_rescore.py --root=.`; `python -m rebar.llm.plan_review.registry regenerate-criteria-guide` (the guide is GENERATED and must not be hand-edited); then `make verify`. Edge: `python -m build --wheel && unzip -l dist/*.whl | grep -c 'evals/'` prints `0`, sdist likewise; `git log --follow evals/plan-review-gate/replay/ledger.jsonl` shows pre-move history.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `docs/experiments` and `docs/calibration` are absent, and `evals/` contains exactly the union of the former `docs/experiments/**` and `docs/calibration/**` files — same total file count as the two trees had before the move, with `docs/calibration/**` now under `evals/calibration/**`.\n- [ ] `git grep -n 'docs/experiments\\|docs/calibration' -- . ':!docs/adr' ':!docs/archive' ':!docs/research' ':!CHANGELOG.md' ':!docs/release-notes.md' ':!tests/fixtures' ':!.test_durations' ':!evals'` prints nothing.\n- [ ] `git diff --stat -M origin/main` shows renames plus only the edits enumerated in Approach.\n- [ ] The wheel contains no `evals/` entry, and the sdist contains no `evals/` entry.\n- [ ] `.github/codeql/codeql-config.yml` lists `evals/**` under `paths-ignore`.\n- [ ] `git diff -U0 -- docs/README.md` has exactly two hunks (lines 129 and 141).\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_docs_index.py` exits 0, proving no `docs/*.md` relative link still points into the vacated trees.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/evals/test_evals_corpus_root.py::test_no_hard_coded_roots` passes against the moved tree, and that module carries no `docs/experiments` literal.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.\n"}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793097788086336001,"uuid":"743a7b40-93e5-4536-8bff-9e4c19849b86"}